ef 1078 #edb/ref 17592186473261 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474025 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0b57ac4-5833-5f98-85f6-8d01d8cfbdee" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186473262 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186473263 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1077 "II" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186473262 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474026 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "99f96f24-dff3-5ad2-ae8b-117ac4e4cad2" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186473264 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186473265 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1077 "III" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186473264 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186474027 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "85b6a004-2b46-516a-adc3-ac69774aa23d" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477860 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477860 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477860 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "435fbf66-881a-599f-a5de-59147174d9f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477872 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477872 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477872 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "469b4926-a18a-5a39-87cf-c8473bed4b47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478013 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478013 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "89babb92-9de9-5f2f-b11d-064346a1f1ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478033 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99e2c243-585a-5ab6-a643-ace8c4066e27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478064 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478064 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478064 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "abf4ed0d-fc7b-5e79-816f-b20987508d59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186477860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186477872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186477872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478262 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1eb96924-1d1d-506d-a661-5befdb8dbe4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1071 "The set $B$ and its boundary $∂B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<1\\},\\,∂B=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The point $P(\\sqrt{2},1)$ lies on the boundary of $B$\n\nII. The point $P(\\sqrt{2},1)$ belongs to $B$\n\nIII. The point $Q(0,-1)$ is an interior point of $B$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5330869-80f9-574d-be15-bcaa4f259731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478455 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n\\{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta \\}\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $B$ consists of all points that lie inside the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/97/97ded2e99adb83b69bc547cef822c46ac2134d3ed17c9cdf65f24083560afae5.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(\\sqrt{2},1)$ and $Q(0,-1)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/38/38a11d6712843367b08ff98843b3c3daf43729d82adbe70e15b8019fb68cee6c.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of $P(\\sqrt{2},1)$ satisfy the equation $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $∂B,$ the boundary of $B.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The coordinates of $P(\\sqrt{2},1)$ do not satisfy the inequality $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<1.$ Hence, $P$ does not belongs to $B.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $Q$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $Q$ that is fully contained inside the set $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and III only'." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
